<title>JAPAN: Koa Oil Osaka refinery to close in May for checks.</title>
<headline>Koa Oil Osaka refinery to close in May for checks.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koa Oil Co Ltd said on Wednesday it would close its Osaka refinery in May for routine maintenance work.</p>
<p>Koa Oil's Osaka refinery turnaround schedule is as follows:</p>
<p>Facility		   Capacity		    Date</p>
<p>			 (barrels per day)</p>
<p>Crude distillation</p>
<p>  unit		     104,000	     May 17 - June 21</p>
<p>Vacuum distillation     55,000	     May 17 - June 20</p>
<p>Catalytic cracker	 25,000	     May 22 - June 24</p>
<p>Alkylation		   8,000	     May  8 - July 1</p>
<p>Catalytic reformer	14,000	     May 17 - June 21</p>
<p>Naphtha desulphuriser   15,000	     May 17 - June 20</p>
<p>Kerosene/gas oil</p>
<p>  desulphuriser no.1    25,000	     May  9 - June 27</p>
<p>		    no.2    21,000	     May  8 - June 30</p>
<p>Indirect desulphuriser  15,000	     May 12 - June 26</p>
<p>The Marifu refinery, which has a 127,000 bpd topper, is not scheduled to close for maintenance work during the fiscal year ending March 31, 1998.</p>
<p>Koa Oil is owned 50 percent by Caltex Petroleum Corp, which is a joint venture of Texaco Inc and Chevron Corp.</p>
</text>
